{
  "id": "bigville_action_container",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R78/R79 (blocks 397000, 400000): CONTAINERS with VOLUME capacity, MULTIPLE contents, and FLUIDS. A container holds several inner Stocks (one per kind); cf_fill moves a commodity in if it FITS by VOLUME (Sum of qty*volume over all contents <= capacity) -- so a bulky item fills a barrel faster than a dense one, and a barrel can hold many things at once. A FLUID (water/ale/oil/milk) only goes in a WATERTIGHT vessel (a barrel/bucket, not a sack/chest). cf_empty takes it back; ck_lock/ck_unlock via a key. Items carry weight + volume as data.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "cf_fill",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "FILL a container from the store: an actor fill-armed, a container holding an inner Stock of the SAME kind, and a store Stock of that kind. Moves fill_amount if (a) the store has it, (b) it FITS by VOLUME -- total contents volume (Sum of qty*volume across ALL the container's contents, so it can hold MANY kinds) + amount*item_volume <= capacity, and (c) a FLUID only goes in a WATERTIGHT vessel. All-or-nothing (no partial); conserved; lock+key gated. WEIGHT drives LOAD: it must also fit by weight (total contents weight + amount*weight <= max_load) -- so a person carries little, a horse-drawn cart carries a lot.",
